            </p>
        </CalloutCard>
        <CalloutCard title="Application Alert!">
            <p>
                <a href = "/dyn/capsizing_ships">Ship stability</a> uses <strong> Center of mass </strong> by ensuring the centers of gravity and bouyancy are in proper locations to avoid capsizing when out at sea.
            </p>
            <p>
                <Image alt = "The MV Golden Ray" src = "/dyn/rigid_body_kinetics/Capsized_ship.jpg" width = 5> The MV Golden Ray</Image>
                In 2019, center of gravity and bouyancy calculations were done incorrectly, resulting in the MV Golden Ray to capsize just off the coast of Brunswick, Georgia.  
            </p>
        </CalloutCard>
    </CalloutContainer>

  </SubSection>

    <SubSection title = "Solution steps" id = "solution_steps">
        The steps involved in analyzing a rigid body mechanical system with Newton's equations are as follows.
        <DisplayEquation equation = `\\begin{align} &1. \\ \\text{System diagram: draw a system diagram.} \\\\
            &2. \\ \\text{FBD: draw a free body diagram.} \\\\
            &3. \\ \\text{Kinematics: determine } \\vec{a}_c, \\vec{a}. \\\\
            &4. \\ \\text{Kinetics: use} \\sum \\vec{F} = m \\vec{a}_c, \\sum M_{CZ} = I_{CZ} \\alpha_Z. \\\\
            &5. \\ \\text{Algebra: rearrange and solve as needed.} \\end{align}` background = "True"/>
        <Example title = "Pendulum" id = "pendulum">
            <div class = "d-flex flex-row">
                <div class = "w-50">
                    Consider the 2D pendulum with a rigid rod of length <InlineEquation equation = "l" /> and mass <InlineEquation equation = "m."/>
                    What is the equation of angular acceleration <InlineEquation equation = "\\alpha" /> as a fuction of <InlineEquation equation = "\\theta, \\dot{\\theta}?"/>
                </div>
                <div class = "w-50">
                    <Image src = "/dyn/rigid_body_kinetics/pendulum.png" width = "5"/>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div slot = "solution">
                <p>
                    <strong>1. System diagram:</strong> The following is the system diagram for the pendulum.
                    Use the polar coordinate system with theta defined as shown.
                </p>
                <Image src = "/dyn/rigid_body_kinetics/pendulum_system_diagram.png" width = "5"/>
                <p>
                    <strong>2. FBD:</strong> The following is the free body diagram for the pendulum.
                </p>
                <Image src = "/dyn/rigid_body_kinetics/pendulum_fbd.png" width = "5"/>
                <p>
                    The following forces are on the free body diagram.
                    <DisplayEquation equation = `\\begin{align} F_O &= F_{O} \\hat{e}_r + F_{O} \\hat{e}_{\\theta} \\\\
                    \\vec{F}_g &= F_g \\cos \\theta \\hat{e}_r - F_g \\sin \\theta \\hat{e}_{\\theta} \\\\ 
                    &= m g \\cos \\theta \\hat{e}_r - m g \\sin \\theta \\hat{e}_{\\theta} \\end{align}`/>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>3. Kinematics:</strong> <InlineEquation equation = "\\vec{a}_c, \\vec{\\alpha}"/>
                    <DisplayEquation equation = `\\begin{align} \\vec{\\alpha} &= \\alpha_z \\hat{k} \\\\
                        \\vec{a}_c &= (\\ddot{r} - r \\dot{\\theta} ^ 2) \\hat{e}_r + (r \\ddot{\\theta} + 2 \\dot{r} \\dot{\\theta}) \\hat{e}_{\\theta} \\\\
                        &= -\\frac{l}{2} \\dot{\\theta} ^ 2 \\hat{e}_r + \\frac{l}{2} \\ddot{\\theta} \\hat{e}_{\\theta} \\end{align}`/>
                    Also, the following equation is true.
                    <DisplayEquation equation = "\\alpha_z = \\ddot{\\theta}"/>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>4. Kinetics:</strong> <InlineEquation equation = "\\sum \\vec{F} = m \\vec{a}_c, \\sum M_{CZ} = I_{CZ} \\alpha_Z"/> where <InlineEquation equation = "c"/> is the center of mass or <InlineEquation equation = "\\sum M_{OZ} = I_{OZ} \\alpha_Z"/> where <InlineEquation equation = "O"/> is a fixed point.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Using <InlineEquation equation = "\\sum M_{OZ} = I_{OZ} \\alpha_Z"/> eliminates the reaction forces at point <InlineEquation equation = "O."/>
                    <DisplayEquation equation = `\\begin{align} \\sum M_{OZ} &= I_{OZ} \\alpha_{Z} \\\\
                        &= -m g \\frac{l}{2} \\sin \\theta \\end{align}`/>
                    Also, the following equation is true.
                    <DisplayEquation equation = "I_{OZ} = \\frac{1}{3} m l ^ 2"/>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>5. Algebra:</strong>
                    <DisplayEquation equation = `\\begin{align} I_{OZ} \\alpha_Z &= -m g \\frac{l}{2} \\sin \\theta \\\\
                        \\frac{1}{3} m l ^ 2 \\ddot{\\theta} &= -m g \\frac{l}{2} \\sin \\theta \\end{align}`/>
                    Solving for <InlineEquation equation = "\\ddot{\\theta}"/> gives the following expression.
                    <DisplayEquation equation = `\\begin{align} \\ddot{\\theta} &= -\\frac{3 g}{2 l} \\sin \\theta \\\\
                        \\alpha(\\theta, \\dot{\\theta}) &= -\\frac{3 g}{2 l} \\sin \\theta \\end{align}`/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </Example>
    </SubSection>

